::heading level=1 id=block-reference
Block Reference
::end

::paragraph id=block-reference-summary
Every block type the parser reads and the renderer draws. `docs/dx-format-contract.dx` is the authority on the format itself; this page is the catalog you can see.
::end

::html id=block-type-table
<table>
	<thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Attributes beyond <code>id</code> and <code>class</code></th><th>What it renders as</th></tr></thead>
	<tbody>
		<tr><td>heading</td><td>level</td><td>A heading; the level is clamped to 1&ndash;4.</td></tr>
		<tr><td>paragraph</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>Body prose. A blank line inside it becomes a line break.</td></tr>
		<tr><td>quote</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>Set in from a margin rule, in italic.</td></tr>
		<tr><td>bulleted-list / numbered-list</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>A list; two spaces of indent nests an item.</td></tr>
		<tr><td>checklist</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>One <code>[x]</code> or <code>[ ]</code> line per item, ticked in the margin.</td></tr>
		<tr><td>nav</td><td>label</td><td>Named targets. An empty body means this document's own headings.</td></tr>
		<tr><td>code</td><td>lang, run, deps, timeout, format</td><td>Monospace source. <code>run</code> makes it executable; <code>format</code> says its output is markup.</td></tr>
		<tr><td>output</td><td>for, status, exit, hash, format</td><td>What a run produced. A failure is the only one called out.</td></tr>
		<tr><td>html</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>Author markup, rendered through the allow-list in <code>render::escape</code>.</td></tr>
		<tr><td>svg</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>A drawing, sanitized the same way. Paint it <code>currentColor</code>.</td></tr>
		<tr><td>board</td><td>height</td><td>This document's own blocks on a canvas. One <code>- id x= y= w= h= to=</code> line per node.</td></tr>
		<tr><td>view</td><td>src, width, height</td><td>A sibling coded page, shown as the page it renders to inside a frame whose <code>sandbox</code> stays empty — shown, never run.</td></tr>
		<tr><td>mermaid / graph</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>Not a kept kind: a flowchart the parser can read arrives as a <code>board</code> plus one hidden block per node (the section below); anything it cannot read stays exactly as written.</td></tr>
		<tr><td>image</td><td>src, alt</td><td>A figure, with the caption as its alt text.</td></tr>
		<tr><td>rule</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>A horizontal rule.</td></tr>
		<tr><td>script</td><td>type, src, module</td><td>No visible body. A JSON one feeds <code>{{name}}</code> in prose.</td></tr>
		<tr><td>style / stylesheet</td><td>media, href</td><td>No visible body. The document's own CSS, always applied.</td></tr>
	</tbody>
</table>
::end

::paragraph id=block-reference-hidden
Any block may carry `hidden`, which keeps it in the source and out of the page. Any block may carry `class`. An unrecognized type is read as a paragraph rather than discarded, so a document written by a newer `dx` never loses its text here.
::end

::heading level=2 id=block-reference-shape-heading
The shape of one block
::end

::svg id=block-reference-svg
<svg viewBox="0 0 720 190" role="img" aria-label="A block is an opening line naming its type and attributes, a verbatim body, and a closing end line">
	<g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" stroke-opacity="0.45">
		<path d="M20 34 L700 34 M20 96 L700 96 M20 150 L700 150"/>
	</g>
	<g fill="currentColor" font-family="monospace" font-size="13">
		<text x="20" y="26">::code id=stats lang=python run</text>
		<text x="20" y="88">print(1)</text>
		<text x="20" y="142">::end</text>
	</g>
	<g fill="currentColor" fill-opacity="0.5" font-family="monospace" font-size="11" text-anchor="end">
		<text x="700" y="26">type, then attributes</text>
		<text x="700" y="88">body, kept exactly as written</text>
		<text x="700" y="142">one closing line, alone</text>
	</g>
	<text x="20" y="178" fill="currentColor" fill-opacity="0.5" font-family="monospace" font-size="11">one blank line separates blocks; the writer never puts a block on one line</text>
</svg>
::end

