::heading level=2 id=block-reference-live-heading
Five kinds, worn by this page
::end

::paragraph id=block-reference-live
The hairline above is a ::rule block. The figure below is an ::image naming a file beside this document, embedded at render time so the page travels whole. The frame after it is a ::view of site/index.html — a coded page shown as the page it renders to, inside a frame whose sandbox stays empty. And the small caps on the table header are this document's own ::style block at work: a style block renders nothing and dresses everything. Below it is the other half of that family, a ::stylesheet — the linked form, naming `block-reference.css` beside this file with `media=print`, so the sheet arrives as an `@import` the page honours only when it is printed.
::end

::image id=block-reference-figure src=figures/block-anatomy.png
The anatomy of one block, exported from this very page by dx png --block.
::end

::view id=block-reference-welcome src=site/index.html height=340

::end

::style id=block-reference-style
.dx-doc table thead th { font-variant-caps: small-caps; letter-spacing: 0.04em; }
::end

::stylesheet id=block-reference-sheet href=block-reference.css media=print

::end
